d  each other one person happened to fall  hit their head on something and died so  when we say do I support life in prison  without parole for murderers in general  again the answer is to say it all  cases is not something that I can get  behind and we need to really apply more  critical thinking more nuanced and quite  frankly I don't this is not to attack  this question from Sam because it's a  perfectly reasonable question I think  that unless we are able to step back  from these sort of principles only  analyses of politics as I've and and  society and culture as I've said before  we're not really going to get anywhere  and figuring out real circumstances that  exist in the complex real world and this  is why I've been critical of the  principles only movement there are  movements online I won't name them many  of you know which ones they are which  say we'll all that matters is principles  we value liberty above all else really  well what do you mean by above all else  because we can pretty quickly come up  with some situations in which you might  go back and say well yeah but that now  Liberty needs to be sort of couched in a  particular way or narrowed in a  particular sense it's perfectly  reasonable to come up with a list of  principles precepts and sort of  overarching ideas that govern your  political philosophy and how you  interpret the world around you but most  of the hard work is actually done in  figuring out complex situations that  contradict that have multiple values  that you might find important but that  contradict each other in some way and  that that's the type of thinking I'm  hoping to get more and more people to do
 

